Notebook[{
Cell["InfraPath", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"685ed6e5-a342-4a9b-844a-2a75183cd524"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"125e5042-bd09-433d-9619-102e82199c43"],

Cell["\<\
InfraPath[{walk}] is the unary form (one walk, possibly non-simple); \
InfraPath[{walk1, ..., walkk}] is the multi-realisation form. Inside \
InfraScene, InfraPath[p1, p2, ..., pk] is the step-wise scene-DSL \
constructor: every length-(k-1) walk {v1, ..., vk} with vi in pi and each \
consecutive pair (vi, v_{i+1}) a graph edge (non-simple chains kept). \
FindInfraPath finders return a List of unary InfraPath[{walk}] wrappers; wrap \
that list with InfraPath @ ... to collapse to multi via auto-flatten. \
Rendered like InfraSegment (sequential-edge semantics).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9479254b-3290-49e8-a5ad-345156835e1f"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"11eea309-4ad6-49cf-9284-b843a96369af"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"ba372417-8825-4aa9-9c03-a824c9a4d7d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"61176cf8-7d8d-4161-bf3b-0c95ef0d3f8b"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e49312dc-9b0f-49d5-9b82-02e2ec97ae06"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"811be0c1-30db-43ad-a41c-c32666b07a3b"],

